  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2003-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The graph passes through \\((-1, 0),\\) \\((1, 0),\\) and \\((0, 2).\\) So \\(f(0) = d = 2.\\)\n\nAdding \\[ \\begin{aligned} &f(1) + f(-1) \\\\ &= (a + b + c + d) \\\\ &\\quad {}+ (-a + b - c + d) \\\\ &= 2b + 2d = 0, \\end{aligned} \\] so \\(b = -d = -2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Read off \\(f(-1) = 0,\\) \\(f(1) = 0,\\) and \\(f(0) = 2\\) from the graph",
        "Adding \\(f(1) + f(-1)\\) eliminates \\(a\\) and \\(c,\\) leaving \\(2b + 2d = 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
